<title>USA: Russia's Vimpel shares soar in NYSE debut.</title>
<headline>Russia's Vimpel shares soar in NYSE debut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vimpel-Communications shares surged about 42 percent, up 8-3/4 to 29-1/4, in the market debut of the Russian wireless telecommunications company.</p>
<p>The magnitude of the jump surprised some IPO analysts, who had forecast a less dramatic market premium of two or three points.</p>
<p>Vimpel offered 5.4 million American Depositary shares in the global offering which were priced at $20.50 each. Renaissance Capital Group is the global coordinator of the offering and Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jenrette led the offering in the United States.</p>
</text>
